  "term": "mathematical biology",
  "definition": "Mathematical biology is a research area that uses mathematical models and dynamical systems to study biological processes. In the packet, it is shown through modeling disease transmission, testing properties such as stability and equilibrium, and using simulations to understand behavior and support prediction.",
